    story: Zhang Toothscar was born into a tenement family, where food, debt, and
      shelter were problems children learned to understand too early. As a child,
      Zhang Toothscar lived through a cave garden childhood, learning caution, secrecy,
      and suspicion of outsiders. As a young adult, Zhang Toothscar worked through
      a river barge contract, trading comfort for balance, rope-burned hands, and
      distance from shore. They enter the dojo to choose the arena before the sea
      chooses for them.
